{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/951080-idea-awakened-anchors-truth-and-lie","id":951080,"title":"[Idea] Awakened Anchors - Truth and Lie","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-15T06:53:22-07:00","id":951080,"title":"[Idea] Awakened Anchors - Truth and Lie","content":"So it turns out mages don't have Anchors that differ from the Mortal Virtue and Vice. While this makes perfect sense, as mages are human, it strikes me as a little lazy. The Awakening changes the soul dramatically, giving it a completely new outlook on the world, so wouldn't the basis of their psychology also change it just as dramatically? It'd still be a very human psychology of course, but changed to accommodate their new perspective. So I came up with the idea of Truth and Lie as a mage's Anchors.<br /> <br /> <b>Truth:</b> During the mage's Awakening, their world crumbled in their hands. The limitations they worked under, the pretty lies they told themselves, the assumptions they made to keep themselves sane, cremated in the light of Supernal truth. However, something did survive the purge. In fact, it was emboldened and refined, like a diamond in the rough being cut to perfection. A Truth that was part of the Supernal all along shone as a guiding star to the Watchtower, allowing the mage to mark their name upon it.<br /> <br /> Truth defines the mage's personal connection to the Supernal, the magical part of their personality. It presents a higher calling within the Supernal as a Virtue is to mundane living. But it can also be the Supernal sand they bury their head in like a Sleeper's Vice, causing them to detach from the Fallen World's trappings, leading to hubris as they ignore the world they live in.<br /> <br /> <b>Lie:</b> If a mage had no Fallen chains whatsoever, they would Ascend. Something keeps them down and grounded, preventing them from inhabiting the Supernal. While some view this connection to the Fallen World to be nothing more than a chain, a wise mage knows that a healthy connection to the world around them is important. It's their retained humanity, the serving of humble pie they need.<br /> <br /> Lie defines the mage's personal connection to the Fallen World. It plants their feet on the ground, which can make them drag into petty and meaningless issues like a Vice. On the other hand, it does inform them that they are still human, and therefore must have a connection with others and of the mundane world, generating a calling to home like a Virtue.<br /> <br /> Mechanics-wise, Truth and Lie pack both Virtue and Vice into one Anchor each. As a result, when sticking to the Virtue part of them under great detriment, they gain a full Willpower refresh. When acting on the Vice part of them, they regain a point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> Haven't really thought much past this though, like how Goetia would work under them or how they would change if the mage's soul was taken, which is why I wanted to start a discussion on it. What do you guys think? Pretty good? Needs a bit of work (besides fleshing out the stuff just mentioned, I mean)? Sucks completely? Lemme know, I wanna test this idea out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T07:11:49-07:00","id":951092,"title":"","content":"This needs some examples. Have you checked out Pendragon's Paradigm Conditions? I think they could serve as examples of Truths.<br /> <br /> As for Lies, that's a tough one...how about this?<br /> <br /> <b>Caution: </b>To the Awakened, seeing the branching paths of the future and what thoughts others hide is like gazing out the window. It is easy for them to think that nothing can surprise them. A Mage with this Lie gains 1 willpower point when they successfully use their magic to prevent a disaster, for themselves or others. They regain all willpower points when they prepare for uncertainty without magic, thus reminding themselves that they are still susceptible to failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T23:19:50-07:00","id":952342,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea, I think you're maybe onto something there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T06:09:26-07:00","id":952458,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd like to see some examples for each, but I am too half-asleep right now to contribute any. This idea was already discussed in my table, though the form presented here is more polished. I'd like to see where it goes once there are some examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T17:27:48-07:00","id":952874,"title":"","content":"Some examples of Truths:<br /> <br /> <b>Justice:</b> You Awoke to the ideal of Justice, as the Greeks knew it. For you, justice is an absolute truth, bordering on a law of nature. When you administer justice to others, you refresh Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Compassion:</b> Your Awakening was one of hope, and your heart overflows with it. When you suffer in the interest of helping or protecting others, refresh Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Fury:</b> The Supernal Realms you saw were a roiling maelstrom of perfect forces, revealing to you the truth that you can be unstoppable. When you act with unnecessary violence or forcefulness, replenish Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}